{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495188-mage-settings","id":1495188,"title":"Mage Settings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-18T13:53:49-07:00","id":1495188,"title":"Mage Settings","content":"So we\u2019re probably all familiar with how to make a setting for most vampire games. Choose a city, choose a time period, choose a sect; after that it\u2019s just a matter of choosing where to put Elysium and making characters. While the actual doing of it to create enough material for a chronicle is hard and time-consuming, if someone asked, \u2018how do I make a setting for my vampire game\u2019, I imagine most people on the WoD forums could give them at least a few good tips and solid direction.<br /> <br /> Basically, my question is, how would you all answer that question for a game like Mage? I know that every game is different and is dependent upon unique circumstances, but I like to have an idea of what a gameline\u2019s fleshed out \u2018setting map\u2019 looks like in my head and Mage has always been one of the harder games for me to figure that out for.<br /> <br /> So how do y\u2019all do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T14:34:02-07:00","id":1495192,"title":"","content":"I would suggest something along the lines of the opposite of your stated vampire method.<br /> <br /> First, start with the central dramatic conflict you want to focus on. Do you want a hot war between the Traditions and Technocracy? Do you want do a lot of political jostling between Crafts trying to make the Disparate Alliance work? Do you want to do a spy thriller of rooting out Nephandi infiltrators? Etc<br /> <br /> Then once you have the &quot;sects&quot; part done, you find the location(s) and time period to compliment that. One of the things about Mage, especially if you're running more of a 2e style game (even if you're using M20) is that Mage settings don't have to be as focused on a single city. The great Chantries and mage controlled Realms - before the Avatar Storm hit - had doorways to Nodes that could span dozens of real world locations all over the globe. This is why I suggest focusing on the central conflict you want to focus on first. The ability to travel to dozens of satellite strongholds around the globe magically attached to the central HQ can be very beneficial to some stories, or very difficult on others. Mage has plenty of dials here. And even if you want to keep the focus of the area fairly small, mages can still be fairly mobile within whatever scope you use: A Syndicate controlled Manhattan Construct is not going to have a hard time getting operatives to Albany if they need to exert some pressure on state legislators.<br /> <br /> After that specific locations tend to fall in line as you note: You know which factions are present and in what numbers, so you know what sort of areas they're going to want to have influence over; even if their demands are more complicated than &quot;useful sources of blood.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-20T06:52:38-07:00","id":1495311,"title":"","content":"Well, first of all, let me link you up to an episode of <i>Mage: The Podcast</i> that deals with this very subject: <b><a href=\"http://magethepodcast.com/mage-settings-cities-with-griffin-horn/\" target=\"_blank\">Mage Settings: Cities with Griffin Horn</a></b>. This is similar to your <i>Vampire </i>method, but maybe it addresses some issues you wouldn't worry about for a <i>Vampire </i>game. <br /> <br /> How you go about developing a <i>Mage</i> setting can depend on how powerful the characters are at the beginning. If you limit players to Arete 2 at the outset, then it doesn't have to be very different from <i>Vampire</i> setting development. On the other hand, as soon as players get Arete 3, they have access to Correspondence 3, and fast and easy global travel is within their reach. With Spirit 3, the Umbra is likelier to become a regular feature. At that point, Heavy Arms' ideas will be major considerations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T15:29:05-07:00","id":1512388,"title":"","content":"Seeing how the movie, Lord of Illusion was released a eleven-months after I bought M:tA, from a book-store at a dying-mall, it was enough to rekindle our interests and run a modern-game ('90's); it was alright; didn't catch on.<br /> <br /> It wasn't until a few years later, I reread it and ran a solid fantasy-game. kind of based off of D&amp;D, but it's WoD, so it had to take place in the real-world, (ish), and it was in Ancient-Greece and it was an awesome-game.<br /> <br /> The best part about Mage, is letting the characters use their own creativity to create magical-effects. A lot of use were from the AD&amp;D, spells-school, so, it took some getting used to.<br /> <br /> <br /> Afterthoughts: now, I think of Mage in a new light and how it can be applied to other worlds like Game of Thrones and AD&amp;D's Dark Sun. The magic is the same; just the world is different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T16:51:18-07:00","id":1512392,"title":"","content":"I love blending fantasy and Sci Fi. I ignore the whole &quot;those that live in space/horizon realms/ etc. discorperate&quot; thing. I love blending futuristic and archaic settings. I'm working, in a haphazard way, on a space setting were Earth was in stasis. Thus a developed cluster of Earth colonies are trying to rescue/evacuate the people of Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-25-2023, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T15:46:43-07:00","id":1512783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495188-mage-settings?p=1512388#post1512388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Afterthoughts: now, I think of Mage in a new light and how it can be applied to other worlds like Game of Thrones</div> </div> </div> </div>Song of Ice and Fire is definitely among my favourite literature series. Did you read through all the books from this series ? Most of the characters, stories, descriptions, and chapters are definitely of a wounderous and good quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T16:47:47-07:00","id":1512794,"title":"","content":"Wondrous, even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T20:26:46-07:00","id":1512812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495188-mage-settings?p=1512783#post1512783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Song of Ice and Fire is definitely among my favourite literature series. Did you read through all the books from this series ? Most of the characters, stories, descriptions, and chapters are definitely of a wounderous and good quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only read Dance of the Dragons; in order to get it back to the library on the due-date with a renewal, I had to read fifty-pages a day. It was brutal. I have the other books, but I haven't read them.<br /> <br /> I have A Song of Ice &amp; Fire RPG game, which, has a lot of setting-info that's good for world-building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T12:02:37-07:00","id":1512897,"title":"","content":"For mage setting I like to take a book out of the Civilization games and take a more 4X approach. Pick out a nation or geographic region, and set up cities and nodes.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b <br /> Then populate it with mages fitting the conflicts you want to encourage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T19:53:03-07:00","id":1521940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495188-mage-settings?p=1512897#post1512897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .Civilization games . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be lying if I said I didn't spend a lot of time capturing, and using Civilization's graphics to make RPG-maps; here's one of a Mage (M:tA: Dark Ages), kingdom of a Magocracy. Yes, that is a government of mages. And yes, that is Tolkiens Adunaic language (Byzantine-culture).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://iili.io/qLOINs.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">MAP</a><br /> <br /> Another good game is Age of Wonders; they have, actual, Nodes and Mage-Schools, the, graphics feels more AD&amp;Dish than Mage: the Ascensionish. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T08:16:29-07:00","id":1521981,"title":"","content":"Another alternative setting might involve a post-apocalyptic setting. Plague, war, or whatever has collapsed civilization and the human population. In one of the <b>Storyteller's Guides </b>they gave a guide to how a reduced human population might reduce the difficulty of casting spells. So you could have relatively powerful Mages striving to rebuild society in the ruins. <br /> <br /> This would lead to both furious infighting among mages and attacks from the other supernaturals. I could see the Council of the Traditions wanting a blend, a sort of Jetsons/Star Trek with lots of spirituality. The Technocratic Union (with the exception of the Void Engineers) would hate the spirituality. The Batini want a low tech, religiously conformist, non democratic society. They want that in order to keep control of it to defend it from the Nephandi. The Wu-lung are magically empowered Confucian bureaucrats, they feel most people should be peasants struggling to survive, i.e. traditional China. The Hollow Ones want whatever the latest fashion in revolution demands. <br /> <br /> It would be a wild setting. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T09:28:38-07:00","id":1524391,"title":"","content":"When I start with Mage, I was in high school, so that's what we ran. We played as slightly older high school students and used our city as the setting, and went from there. The adventures happened on about a literal weekly basis, and each session I updated them what the other factions in the city had done, and how they planned to react, to that, or proactivity do something on their own. Is still the most fun I had with the game.<br /> <br /> You can run a Harry Potter Style setting, in a magical university or high school. You can look to Ars Magica and MAge the Sorceror's Crusade too, for other ideas. <br /> <br /> What you need, is:<br /> (1) A hook - why the PC's are working together. <br /> (2) Give them problems, lots of problems. Ideally pick from their background<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 10-22-2023, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}